        {
          "type": "graph",
          "say": "Brute force tries every order: n factorial. But what's left to do depends only on which nodes you've visited, and where you are now. The path zero, one, two costs seven. The path one, zero, two costs thirteen. Both have visited the same set, and both end at node two, so every way to continue is the same for both. Keep only the cheaper one: seven. That's one state: the set, as a bitmask, plus the last node. Extend it to node three for two more: nine, the cheapest way to visit all four, ending at three.",
