    {
      "id": "03",
      "title": "Why O(3^n)?",
      "question": "Looping over every submask of every mask: why is that 3^n and not 4^n?",
      "scenes": [
        {
          "type": "question",
          "say": "Question three. Looping over every submask of every mask: why does that cost three to the n, and not four to the n? Pause and answer out loud.",
          "pauseAfter": 3,
          "props": {
            "question": "Every submask of every mask: why <em>3<sup>n</sup></em>?"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "points",
          "say": "Count the pairs, mask and sub, element by element. Each element is in both, in the mask only, or in neither. It can't be in the sub without the mask. Three choices per element, independently, so three to the n pairs in total. For sixteen elements, that's forty-three million: fine. Four to the sixteen would be four billion.",
          "props": {
            "title": "Three choices per <em>element</em>",
            "items": [
              {
                "at": "both",
                "label": "Both",
                "title": "In mask and in sub",
                "body": "",
                "code": "mask 1, sub 1"
              },
              {
                "at": "only",
                "label": "Mask only",
                "title": "In mask, not in sub",
                "body": "",
                "code": "mask 1, sub 0"
              },
              {
                "at": "neither",
                "label": "Neither",
                "title": "In neither",
                "body": "Never in sub without mask.",
                "code": "mask 0, sub 0"
              },
              {
                "at": "sixteen",
                "label": "n = 16",
                "title": "3<sup>16</sup> ≈ 43 million",
                "body": "4<sup>16</sup> ≈ 4.3 billion."
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "say": "That's the cost of partition problems. Here: split tasks into the fewest work sessions, each no longer than a limit. First, precompute each subset's total load, in O of two to the n: a mask's load is its lowest task, plus the load of the rest. Then d p of m is the fewest sessions for the tasks in m. Try every submask as one session: if it fits, the rest is d p of m minus sub, plus one. Three to the n overall.",
          "props": {
            "title": "Fewest <em>sessions</em>",
            "file": "sessions.cpp",
            "tag": "C++",
            "lang": "cpp",
            "size": 20,
            "width": 1250,
            "code": "int minSessions(const vector<int>& tasks, int limit) {\n    int n = tasks.size(), full = (1 << n) - 1;\n    vector<int> load(1 << n, 0);                  // total time of each subset\n    for (int m = 1; m <= full; ++m)\n        load[m] = load[m & (m - 1)] + tasks[__builtin_ctz(m)];\n    vector<int> dp(1 << n, INT_MAX);              // dp[m]: fewest sessions for m\n    dp[0] = 0;\n    for (int m = 1; m <= full; ++m)\n        for (int sub = m; sub > 0; sub = (sub - 1) & m)   // non-empty sub of m\n            if (load[sub] <= limit && dp[m ^ sub] != INT_MAX)\n                dp[m] = min(dp[m], dp[m ^ sub] + 1);  // sub is one session\n    return dp[full];\n}",
            "highlights": [
              {
                "at": "First",
                "lines": "3-5",
                "note": "Load of every subset, O(2<sup>n</sup>)"
              },
              {
                "at": "fewest",
                "lines": "6-7",
                "note": "dp[m]: fewest sessions for m"
              },
              {
                "at": "submask",
                "lines": "9",
                "note": "Every submask = one session"
              },
              {
                "at": "rest#2",
                "lines": "10-11",
                "note": "If it fits: 1 + dp[rest]"
              },
              {
                "at": "overall",
                "lines": "12",
                "note": "O(3<sup>n</sup>) total"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
